  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The lotteries have quantifiable outcomes and probabilities. Lottery A offers 2400 Euros with 100% probability, so the probability of a favorable outcome is 100%. Lottery B offers 2500 Euros with 33% probability, 2400 Euros with 66% probability, and 0 Euros with 1% probability. If differences between outcomes (e.g., 2400 vs. 2500 Euros) are considered negligible, then any positive outcome (2400 or 2500 Euros) can be treated as 'favorable'. Thus, the probability of a favorable outcome in Lottery B is 33% + 66% = 99%, and in Lottery A it is 100%. The reason would prefer Lottery A, as it has a higher probability (100% vs. 99%) of a favorable outcome.",
