  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes treating non-zero outcomes as negligibly different and choosing based on the higher probability of any favorable (i.e., non-zero) outcome. The individual’s focus on 'avoiding 0' aligns partially with this logic, as it reflects concern about the risk of receiving nothing. However, the report does not indicate whether the individual considered the 2400 and 2500 Euro outcomes as similar or evaluated the overall probability of favorable outcomes. The reasoning appears more loss-averse (focusing on avoiding the worst outcome) than based on maximizing the probability of a favorable one under indifference to outcome differences. While there is a thematic overlap in avoiding zero, the full structure of the decision reason (indifference to outcome differences, comparison of favorable outcome probabilities) is not clearly present in the report. Therefore, it is uncertain whether the specific reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 50
}

